night before last night<div>vorgestern Nacht</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">noun</font></div>person destined to save the universe or world, also called the Chosen One<ol><li><div>Auserkorene</div></li><li><div>Auserwählte</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">adverb</font></div>lately<ol><li><div>kürzlich</div></li><li><div>neulich</div></li><li><div>vor kurzem</div></li><li><div>in letzter Zeit</div></li><li><div>vor ein paar Tagen</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">adverb</font></div>same but with things reversed<div>umgekehrt</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">adverb</font></div><ol><li>in reversed orientation<ol><li><div>andersherum</div></li><li><div>andersrum</div></li></ol></li><li>same but with mentioned things reversed<div>umgekehrt</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>more power can be usurped by writing than fighting<div>die Feder ist mächtiger als die Klinge</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div>understanding is reached, one comprehends<ol><li><div>der Groschen fällt</div></li><li><div>der Groschen ist gefallen</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>When you use a thing too much, it ultimately breaks<div>der Krug geht so lange zum Brunnen, bis er bricht</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>the only real test of something is as what it is intended to be used for<ol><li><div>Probieren geht über Studieren</div></li><li><div>die Praxis wird es zeigen</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div>Pangram<ol><li><div>Franz jagt im komplett verwahrlosten Auto quer durch Bayern</div></li><li><div>zwölf Boxkämpfer jagen Viktor quer über den großen Sylter Deich</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div>used to indicate that one does not need to continue a story<div>der Rest ist Geschichte</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>well-intended acts can lead to disasters<div>der Weg zur Hölle ist mit guten Vorsätzen gepflastert</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">noun</font></div>something considered to be excellent<div>Hammer</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>one often neglects those closest to oneself<div>die Kinder des Schusters haben die schlechtesten Schuhe</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>achieving something is made impossible by frailty<div>der Geist ist willig, aber das Fleisch ist schwach</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">noun</font></div>small additional burden which causes failure<div>der Tropfen, der das Fass zum Überlaufen bringt</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div>shift focus to an overriding point or impediment<div>die Sache ist</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div>the toilet is clogged<div>die Toilette ist verstopft</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>cooking food for a man is a good way to win his affections<div>Liebe geht durch den Magen</div></div><div>/<font color="gray">ðə ˌhoʊl ˌnaɪn ˈjɑɹdz</font>/<br>
