<div><font class="grammar" color="green">noun</font></div>the place in which something happens<ol><li><div>Wo</div></li><li><div>wo</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div>where are we<div>wo sind wir</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div>where are we going?<div>wo gehen wir?</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div>where are you?<ol><li><div>wo bist du?</div></li><li><div>wo sind Sie?</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div>in which country or region were you born or raised<ol><li><div>woher kommen Sie ?</div></li><li><div>woher kommst du ?</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div>where are your parents?<div>wo sind deine Eltern?</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div>where can I find a hotel<div>wo ist hier ein Hotel</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div>where do you live?<ol><li><div>wo wohnen Sie?</div></li><li><div>wo wohnst du?</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div>where does it hurt?<div>wo tut es weh</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div>where does this bus go<div>wohin fährt dieser Bus?</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div>where does this train go<div>wohin fährt dieser Zug?</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div>where have you been?<ol><li><div>wo bist du gewesen?</div></li><li><div>wo sind Sie gewesen?</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div>direct me to the restroom<div>wo ist die Toilette?</div></div><div>/<font color="gray">wɛə-</font>/, /<font color="gray">wɛɚ-</font>/, /<font color="gray">ʍɛə ˌðɛəɹ ɪz ə ˈwɪl ðɛəɹ ɪz ə ˈweɪ</font>/, /<font color="gray">ʍɛɚ ˌðɛɚ ɪz ə ˈwɪl ðɛɚ ɪz ə ˈweɪ</font>/<br>
<div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>if someone wants or wills something strongly enough, a way can be found<ol><li><div>wo ein Wille ist, ist auch ein Weg</div></li><li><div>man muss nur wollen</div></li><li><div>es ist Platz in der kleinsten Hütte</div></li><li><div>wer will, der kann</div></li><li><div>wer will, findet Wege, wer nicht will, findet Gründe</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>if there is a hint of something occurring it could indeed be true, but rumors should be handled with skepticism<div>wo Rauch ist, ist auch Feuer</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div><div>wo brennt's</div></div><div>/<font color="gray">ˈ(h)wɛəɹəˌbaʊts/&lt;q:noun&gt;</font>/, /<font color="gray">ˌ(h)wɛəɹəˈbaʊts/&lt;q:adverb&gt;</font>/<br>
