<div><font class="grammar" color="green">verb</font></div>to address using the more formal second-person pronoun<div>siezen</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>proverb<ol><li><div>man ist, was man isst</div></li><li><div>man ist, was man ißt</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">interjection</font></div>certainly (reply to a request)<ol><li><div>aber hallo</div></li><li><div>und ob</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>It is easier to persuade others with polite requests and a positive attitude rather than with rude demands and negativity<div>mit einem Tropfen Honig fängt man mehr Fliegen als mit einem Fass Essig</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>you can show someone how to do something, but you can't make them do it<div>man kann den Gaul zur Tränke führen, aber saufen muss er selber</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div>that is very true<ol><li><div>das kannst du laut sagen</div></li><li><div>das können Sie laut sagen</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>it is not possible to produce something refined from something which is unrefined<ol><li><div>man kann aus einem Ackergaul kein Rennpferd machen</div></li><li><div>man kann aus einem Esel kein Rennpferd machen</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>phrase<div>wo gehobelt wird, fallen Späne</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>too old to change<div>was Hänschen nicht lernt, lernt Hans nimmermehr</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>one should avoid romantic or sexual relationships in the workplace<div>Bürofick bringt Unglück</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>everything has a price<ol><li><div>alles hat seinen Preis</div></li><li><div>man kriegt nichts geschenkt</div></li><li><div>nur der Tod ist umsonst</div></li><li><div>von nichts kommt nichts</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">interjection</font></div>really? ; no kidding! ; Is that so?<ol><li><div>was Sie nicht sagen</div></li><li><div>was du nicht sagst</div></li><li><div>was ihr nicht sagt</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>quality of goods increases as the prices increases<div>Qualität hat ihren Preis</div></div><div>/<font color="gray">ju hæv ˈbju.tɪ.fəl aɪz</font>/, /<font color="gray">juː hæv ˈbjuː.tɪ.fəl aɪz</font>/<br>
